result_text:
`checkout_github_prs()` now warns and returns normally when no PRs match, instead of raising an exception. I haven't run the tests or the command.

All the changes are in `git_machete/client.py`:
- **`__get_valid_pull_requests`:** these cases now call `warn(...)` instead of raising `MacheteException`:
  - no PRs are open in the repository (`--all`);
  - the current user has no open PRs (`--mine`);
  - the given user has no open PRs (`--by`);
  - an explicitly requested PR number isn't found. This now only warns, even when it's the only PR number given. Before, a single missing number was an error.
  - none of the given PR numbers are found.
- **`checkout_github_prs`:** if no valid PRs come back, it returns right away. It skips the fetch, branch checkout, and annotation sync.

If any existing tests expect these errors, they'll fail now. I left the tests alone, as you asked.
